 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Gently steam them open, then use little oil and lots of brush soap. Turn them upside down after few minutes to air them. That works well too. Whichever way you do it, hitting them dry after cleaning causes them to break. Soak them gently in warm water for half an hour before cleaning. It helps loosen the dried paint. Then a short warm soak in turpentine will save them. Stiff brushes are tricky, you caress them, not push.",
